id: pm-gh1695
title: "GH-1695: accept settings paths and provide bounded config-key recovery"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1695. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,config,"gh:1695",sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T12:23:24.852Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T11:57:32.176Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T11:57:32.176Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Accept every supported settings path as an alias in SDK-backed config get/set without bypassing validation; Unknown keys offer at most three nearest legal keys and a working config-list inspection command; Preserve complete legal keys in structured recovery and reject unknown keys without settings writes
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Supported settings paths and all ten context section leaves use the SDK configuration surface. Grouped and dotted context integer setters plus profile lint/planning share the descriptor rule. Full depth round-trips, and unknown-key SDK errors include declared scoped aliases and paths with a complete inventory retry."
expected_result: Configuration and profiles share validation and persistence; every supported scoped key/path is discoverable without an oversized human refusal.
actual_result: Four intended pre-fix review failures are repaired. All 232 tests across eight files and both linked configuration/profile commands pass; original full-depth failing-before control remains. Typechecks and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx consumers pass; public SDK surface verifies zero classified changes. Changed parser/recovery branches are instrumented without gaps. Complete exact-head CI coverage/static and re-review remain delivery gates; metadata-only discovery is separately tracked open in pm-8txeqe.
